  "outcome_rationale": "Pre-reg H2 was framed as positive direction (urine A > benign A, d > 0.3). Observed: urine A is dramatically LOWER than benign tissue A (mean \u0394A = \u22120.165, paired d = \u22122.39 across all 4 patients). |d|=2.39 is among the largest effect sizes measured anywhere in the EDEAR validation record. The pre-reg explicitly anticipated this case under O5_UNEXPECTED: \"urine vs benign d > 0.3 but in NEGATIVE direction (urine A-score LOWER than benign tissue, suggesting clearance of disrupted cells rather than retention).\" Convening with Heath before deciding card update direction. Numbers reported honestly. Reclassified from O4_URINE_NULL.",
  "observed_pattern": "urine_lower_than_benign_tissue_in_all_4_patients",
  "secondary_observation": "Tumor vs benign paired d = -0.016 in this n=4 cohort \u2014 the expected tumor > benign signal from VAL-058 (n=238, paired d = +0.497) is not visible here. This is consistent with the n=4 sample size precluding stable per-patient tumor signal. However, the urine signal magnitude is 150x larger than the tumor-tissue signal in this same cohort, which is the framework-relevant observation."
